      "text": "1. Find the prime factors of $18$ and $42$:\n   \\[\n   18 = 2 \\cdot 3^2, \\quad 42 = 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 7\n   \\]\n2. Determine the greatest common divisor (GCD) of $18$ and $42$: \n   \\[\n   \\text{GCD}(18, 42) = 2 \\cdot 3 = 6\n   \\]\n3. Determine the least common multiple (LCM) of $18$ and $42$:\n   \\[\n   LCM(18, 42) = 2 \\cdot 3^2 \\cdot 7 = 126\n   \\]\n4. Calculate the product of the GCD and LCM: \n   \\[\n   \\text{GCD}(18, 42) \\times LCM(18, 42) = 6 \\times 126 = \\boxed{756}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of the greatest common divisor and the least common multiple of $18$ and $42$ is $\\boxed{756}$.",
