      "text": "1. **Largest Common Factor:**\n   - To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of $18$ and $42$, we prime factorize both numbers:\n     $$\\begin{align*}\n     18 &= 2^1 \\times 3^2 \\\\\n     42 &= 2^1 \\times 3^1 \\times 7^1\n     \\end{align*}$$\n   - The common prime factors across both numbers are $2^1$ and $3^1$.\n   - The product of these common factors is $2^1 \\times 3^1 = \\boxed{6}$.\n   \n2. **Least Common Multiple:**\n   - To find the least common multiple (LCM) of $18$ and $42$, we combine the highest powers of the prime factors:\n     $$\\begin{align*}\n     18 &= 2^1 \\times 3^2 \\\\\n     42 &= 2^1 \\times 3^1 \\times 7^1\n     \\end{align*}$$\n   - The LCM comprises all prime factors, each raised to the highest power they occur in either number:\n     $$\\begin{align*}\n     \\text{LCM} &= 2^1 \\times 3^2 \\times 7^1 \\\\\n     \\text{LCM} &= 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 7 \\\\\n     \\text{LCM} &= 2 \\times 9 \\times 7 \\\\\n     \\text{LCM} &= 126\n     \\end{align*}$$\n\n3. **GCD and LCM Producto:**\n   - Now, to find their product:\n     $$\\begin{align*}\n     \\text{GCD} \\times \\text{LCM} &= 6 \\times 126 \\\\\n     &= 126 \\times (6 / 6 \\times 7) \\\\\n     &= 756\n     \\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, the product of the GCD and LCM is $\\boxed{756}$.",
